## Part I: While Loops

## 1. Write a while loop that prints the numbers from 1 through 10, onenumber per line.
x = 1
while x <= 10:
    print(x)
    x += 1

## 2. Write a program using a while loop that calculates the sum of all integers from 1 through 50. Print the final sum.
current_number = 1
sum = 0
while current_number <= 50:
    sum += current_number
    current_number += 1
print(sum)

## 3. Write a program that repeatedly asks the user to enter a password.
## The correct password is "python123".
## Continue asking until the user enters the correct password.
## When the correct password is entered, print "Access Granted".
password = ""
while password != "python123":
    password = input("Enter a password\n")
print("Access Granted")

